<main class="container py-5" style="max-width: 850px">
    <div class="card shadow-sm"><div class="card-body p-4 p-md-5">
        <p class="text-muted small">Barangay San Jose Blotter Management System</p>
        <h1 class="h3 mb-4">Privacy Notice</h1>
        <p>The Barangay San Jose office handles personal information for incident recording, assessment, proceedings, official documentation, and related administrative reporting. Republic Act No. 10173, the Data Privacy Act of 2012, provides the framework for protecting this information.</p>
        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Information and purpose</h2>
        <p>Records may include identity and contact details, addresses, case-party information, incident accounts, hearing records, outcomes, and system activity. Information should be relevant to the particular barangay service. Ask the Secretary which details are required for your transaction.</p>
        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Access and sharing</h2>
        <p>Authorized personnel access records according to their assigned roles and cases. Information may be disclosed to a legally authorized receiving agency when necessary for official action. Optional email updates use the verified address agreed to by the party; the mail provider processes the short message for delivery. Other parties' names and allegations are excluded from these advisories.</p>
        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Safeguards and retention</h2>
        <p>The application uses individual accounts, role restrictions, activity records, and encrypted backup files. The barangay remains responsible for secure devices, hosting, backup custody, and applying an approved retention and disposal schedule. Ask the office for the retention period and policy applicable to your record.</p>
        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Requests and choices</h2>
        <p>Contact the Barangay San Jose office or Secretary for its designated privacy contact, to request access or correction, to ask about the lawful grounds for processing, or to raise a privacy concern. Requests are assessed under applicable law and recordkeeping obligations. You may also raise concerns with the <a href="https://privacy.gov.ph/" rel="noopener noreferrer">National Privacy Commission</a>.</p>
        <p>You may decline or discontinue optional email updates through the office. This choice does not by itself prevent lawful official recordkeeping or replace the service of required notices and summons.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-outline-primary mt-2" href="{{ auth()->check() ? route('dashboard') : route('login') }}">Back to System</a>
    </div></div>
</main></body></html>
